<title>MEXICO: Empresas ICA building Pemex natgas plant.</title>
<headline>Empresas ICA building Pemex natgas plant.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican builder Empresas ICA was awarded the construction project for a natural gas processing plant in Ciudad Pemex, Pemex officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>Construction for the plant was said to be $172 million and was scheduled to be finished by March 1999.  </p>
<p>ICA and its partner Fluor Daniel also constructed another criogenic plant, which began operations last month in Reforma, Chiapas. Both plants replace sites destroyed in a blast a year ago at the nearby Cactus natural gas complex.</p>
<p>The plants each have the capacity to process 600 million cubic feet per day (cfd) of natural gas.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
</text>
